# omp 17.3.7 `--mode rpc` APPROVAL dialog (agent -> host), in wire order — the frame family that
# deadlocks a host which does not answer it.
#
# Provenance: q3-probe5-always-ask.txt (the stall, captured under `--approval-mode always-ask`)
# and q3-probe6-unblock.txt (the same run answered). Both were driven credential-free against a
# local stub model. VERBATIM unless marked RECONSTRUCTED.
#
# <- q3-probe3-hosttool-roundtrip.txt:37. A second fire-and-forget setWidget, emitted mid-run.
#    It is answered by nobody in the probe and blocks nothing (BLOCKING_UI_REQUESTS 0).
{"type":"extension_ui_request","id":"155cddcfa181ec58","method":"setWidget","widgetKey":"autoresearch"}
# <- q3-probe5-always-ask.txt:10 (restated at :16 as the blocking request). THE STALL FRAME.
#    Note what is ABSENT: a `timeout` field. requestRpcDialog arms a timer ONLY when
#    opts.timeout !== undefined (rpc-mode.ts:640), so this dialog waits forever — the probe
#    measured 45s of wall clock with no agent_end and had to kill the child. The tool name is
#    carried in the title's first line; `options` are the exact labels an answer may name.
{"type":"extension_ui_request","id":"155cde478590975d","method":"select","title":"Allow tool: bash\nCommand: echo EDEN_APPROVAL_PROBE","options":["Approve","Deny"]}
# <- q3-probe5-always-ask.txt:11. Emitted BEFORE any answer arrives — proof that a
#    tool_execution_start says nothing about whether the tool was authorized.
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_bash_1","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"echo EDEN_APPROVAL_PROBE"}}
# <- q3-probe6-unblock.txt:26 (the F-answer-deny arm). Answering {"value":"Deny"} makes the tool
#    fail with a denial result and the TURN CONTINUES to a clean agent_end and exit 0 — a deny
#    is not a transport fault. (The A-answer-approve arm at q3-probe6-unblock.txt:5 returns the
#    real command output with isError false.)
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_bash_1","toolName":"bash","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool call denied by user: bash"}],"details":{}},"isError":true}
